> I'm using Ubuntu 24.04. Could you agian let me know how to run cmake/

● On Ubuntu 24.04, here's how to install and run CMake:

  Installing CMake

  # Update package list
  sudo apt update

  # Install CMake
  sudo apt install cmake

  # Verify installation
  cmake --version

  Ubuntu 24.04 should have CMake 3.28+ which is perfect for SLIM.

  Running CMake with SLIM

  # Navigate to your project
  cd /home/ueda/slim-cmake

  # Set up LMNtal compiler path (required)
  export LMNTAL_HOME=/path/to/your/lmntal/compiler

  # Option 1: Use the convenient build script
  ./build-cmake.sh

  # Option 2: Manual CMake build
  mkdir build && cd build
  cmake ..
  make -j$(nproc)

  # Option 3: Debug build
  ./build-cmake.sh --debug

  # Option 4: Developer build with extra warnings
  ./build-cmake.sh --devel

  Testing the Build

  # After building, test the executable
  cd /home/ueda/slim-cmake/build-test
  ./src/slim --help

  # Run tests (if you have LMNTAL_HOME set)
  make test

  Build Options

  # In build directory
  cmake .. -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release     # Optimized build
  cmake .. -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug       # Debug build
  cmake .. -DENABLE_DEBUG=ON              # Enable debug features
  cmake .. -DENABLE_TCMALLOC=ON           # Use tcmalloc

  The CMake system I set up is ready to go - just install cmake and run ./build-cmake.sh!

